From 0e8b12995807a23ecc0aa76308f55b51cce25c28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeremy Roman <jbroman@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:39:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [159] Allow cross-world serialization from detached realms

Original change's description:
> Allow cross-world serialization from detached realms
>
> Extensions such as Tampermonkey construct cross-world CustomEvents using
> primordials captured from a sandboxed iframe that is removed immediately
> after setup. Failing closed whenever the source realm's execution
> context is detached caused object event details on those events to
> become null in isolated worlds.
>
> Allow cross-world serialization to proceed in the source realm as long
> as its V8 context is still alive, while avoiding null execution context
> dereferences in the serializer and continuing to disallow
> SharedArrayBuffer and shared JavaScript value sharing when the source
> execution context is no longer valid.
>
